<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Internet Programming - CO1</title>

    <style>
        body{
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin:0;
            background:#f4f4f4;
        }
        header{
            background:#0066cc;
            color:white;
            padding:20px;
            text-align:center;
        }
        nav{
            background:#333;
            padding:10px;
            text-align:center;
        }
        nav a{
            color:white;
            text-decoration:none;
            margin:15px;
        }
        section{
            background:white;
            margin:20px;
            padding:20px;
            border-radius:8px;
            box-shadow:0 0 5px gray;
        }
        pre{
            background:#f0f0f0;
            padding:10px;
            border-left:5px solid #0066cc;
            overflow:auto;
        }
        footer{
            background:#0066cc;
            color:white;
            text-align:center;
            padding:15px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<header>
    <h1>Internet Programming</h1>
    <p>Standards-Compliant HTML/XHTML, XML & HTTP</p>
</header>

<nav>
    <a href="#html">HTML</a>
    <a href="#xml">XML</a>
    <a href="#http">HTTP</a>
</nav>

<section id="html">
    <h2>HTML5 Web Page</h2>
    <p>
        HTML is the standard markup language used to create web pages.
        It provides headings, paragraphs, images, tables, forms, and links.
    </p>
</section>

<section id="xml">
    <h2>XML Example</h2>

<pre>
&lt;student&gt;
    &lt;name&gt;John&lt;/name&gt;
    &lt;course&gt;Internet Programming&lt;/course&gt;
    &lt;year&gt;2026&lt;/year&gt;
&lt;/student&gt;
</pre>

</section>

<section id="http">
    <h2>HTTP Communication</h2>

    <ol>
        <li>User enters a website URL.</li>
        <li>DNS converts the domain name into an IP address.</li>
        <li>Browser sends an HTTP request.</li>
        <li>Server processes the request.</li>
        <li>Server returns an HTTP response.</li>
        <li>Browser displays the web page.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Sample HTTP Response</h3>

<pre>
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: text/html
Content-Length: 1024
Connection: keep-alive
</pre>

</section>

<section>
    <h2>Features of a Standards-Compliant Web Page</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>Uses HTML5 DOCTYPE.</li>
        <li>Semantic elements (header, nav, section, footer).</li>
        <li>Proper nesting and closing of tags.</li>
        <li>Responsive viewport meta tag.</li>
        <li>Valid HTML structure.</li>
    </ul>

</section>

<footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Internet Programming Lab | HTML5 Example</p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
